  "exact_bilingual_source": "# 00000001277\n\n**English.** Definition: The entropy-rate extremum of a k-th order Markov chain is the maximal entropy under given transition constraints. Conjecture: The transition support of the entropy-maximizing chain is a partial permutation matrix; and the extremum is given explicitly by the permutation-block decomposition of the admissible matrix. (transition-constraint entropy maximum)\n\n**中文。** 定义：k 阶马尔可夫链的熵率极值为给定转移约束下的最大熵。猜想：熵极大链的转移支撑为部分置换矩阵；且极值由允许矩阵的置换块分解显式给出。（转移约束熵极大）\n",
  "source_scope_notes": [
    "Both languages explicitly claim that the transition support of an entropy-maximizing chain is a partial permutation matrix. The source does not state a restriction excluding full admissible transition supports or a restriction on the number of states.",
    "A formal counterexample must establish an actual admissible entropy-maximizing Markov chain and its support under a clearly specified transition constraint; merely presenting positive entropy does not establish maximality.",
    "Refuting the support clause would negate the conjunction without needing to adjudicate the claimed permutation-block formula. No proof implementation or mathematical validation was performed in this eligibility task."
  ],
